% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `channel`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  The class text is PRINTED
% SOURCE, not ours: TM-100 Figure 3.7 "Part of class 'channel'" (PDF p15,
% printed folio 13), as transcribed in
% docs/simpos/printed/listings/tm0100_p15.esp, verbatim (layout as
% printed).  The figure is "part of" the class: SIMPOS's full `channel`
% is lost.
%
% The figure prints no :create.  `:create(#channel, C)` (held callers:
% kappa2 kernel/flm/VOL1.ESP:52; pimscsi's slot initialisers) is the
% PRINTED stream:create/2 (TM-100 Fig. 3.6), inherited through the
% printed nature.  The printed slot `post_queue` overrides stream's slot
% of the same name (TM-100 p15 prose: "the slot 'post_queue' is
% overridden in the channel"); its class, post_queue_for_message, is an
% INTERPOLATED stand-in (post_queue_for_message.esp).
%
% Not stood in: the 2-argument send/2 and receive/2 of TR-056 p14's
% printed interface (docs/simpos/printed/listings/TR-056_p14.esp), which
% kappa2 kernel/itr/ITRTCM.ESP sends; and set_sender/2, get_sender/2 of
% class `message` ("A message is defined by class 'message'", TM-100
% p15), which the printed send/3 and receive/3 call.  kl0 refuses them
% as SIMPOS calls.

    class  channel  has

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.7, PDF p15 (the nature)
    nature      stream;

    instance

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.7, PDF p15 (the overriding slot)
    attribute ( post_queue  :=
                        Queue :- :create(#post_queue_for_message, Queue) );
                    % Overrides 'post_queue' of class 'stream'

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.7, PDF p15
    :send(Channel, Message, Sender) :-
            :set_sender(Message, Sender),
            :put(Channel, Message);

    % PRINTED: TM-100 Fig. 3.7, PDF p15
    :receive(Channel, Message, Sender) :-
            :get(Channel, Message),
            :get_sender(Message, Sender);

    end.
